1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,350
You walk up to the pull-up bar.

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:03,930
Everyone's watching.

3
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:05,790
You jump, you grab it,

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:06,870
and nothing.

5
00:00:06,970 --> 00:00:08,590
You just hang there,

6
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:10,110
like a wet towel.

7
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:11,690
Twenty seconds of kicking.

8
00:00:11,690 --> 00:00:13,160
Zero pull-ups.

9
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,360
Here's the thing.

10
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:16,020
It's not your arms.

11
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,340
Most people fail the pull-up for three

12
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:20,640
reasons, and none of them is weak

13
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,610
biceps.

14
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:23,970
Fix those three, and in about thirty

15
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:26,290
days you can do your first one.

16
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:28,110
Stay to the end for the exact

17
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:28,860
plan.

18
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,010
Reason one.

19
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:32,160
Your grip gives up before your back

20
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,900
does.

21
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,860
If you can't hold your own body

22
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,500
weight for thirty seconds,

23
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,420
your hands quit first.

24
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,410
So start with the dead hang.

25
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:43,520
Grab the bar, arms straight,

26
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:44,670
and just hang.

27
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:45,960
Thirty seconds.

28
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,270
Three times.

29
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:48,310
Every day.

30
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:49,280
That's it?

31
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,290
Just hanging?

32
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:51,510
Just hanging.

33
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,200
It's harder than it looks.

34
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,380
Reason two.

35
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,190
You pull with your arms.

36
00:00:56,270 --> 00:00:58,890
But a pull-up is a back exercise.

37
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:02,060
Your lats, the big wings on your

38
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,850
back, are supposed to start the move.

39
00:01:05,651 --> 00:01:07,471
Here's how you wake them up.

40
00:01:07,551 --> 00:01:10,071
Hang, then pull your shoulders down,

41
00:01:10,071 --> 00:01:11,521
away from your ears,

42
00:01:11,521 --> 00:01:13,321
without bending your arms.

43
00:01:13,421 --> 00:01:14,941
It's a tiny move.

44
00:01:15,021 --> 00:01:17,131
Ten of those, three sets.

45
00:01:17,231 --> 00:01:18,261
Reason three.

46
00:01:18,341 --> 00:01:20,191
You only practise the way up,

47
00:01:20,191 --> 00:01:21,501
which you can't do yet.

48
00:01:22,501 --> 00:01:24,151
But your muscles are stronger on the

49
00:01:24,151 --> 00:01:26,031
way down than on the way up.

50
00:01:26,131 --> 00:01:27,501
So jump to the top,

51
00:01:27,501 --> 00:01:28,891
chin over the bar,

52
00:01:28,891 --> 00:01:31,181
and lower yourself as slowly as you

53
00:01:31,181 --> 00:01:31,961
can.

54
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:33,561
Five seconds down.

55
00:01:33,661 --> 00:01:35,361
These are called negatives,

56
00:01:35,361 --> 00:01:36,931
and they are the fastest way to

57
00:01:36,931 --> 00:01:38,161
your first pull-up.

58
00:01:38,261 --> 00:01:40,391
So I cheat on the way up?

59
00:01:40,491 --> 00:01:42,311
You skip the part you can't do,

60
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:43,931
and train the part you can.

61
00:01:44,031 --> 00:01:45,301
So here's the plan.

62
00:01:45,381 --> 00:01:46,691
Three days a week.

63
00:01:47,691 --> 00:01:50,421
Dead hangs, three times thirty seconds.

64
00:01:50,501 --> 00:01:52,911
Shoulder pulls, three sets of ten.

65
00:01:52,991 --> 00:01:55,021
Negatives, three sets of three,

66
00:01:55,021 --> 00:01:56,411
five seconds each.

67
00:01:56,511 --> 00:01:57,621
And a bonus.

68
00:01:57,701 --> 00:01:59,611
Rows under a sturdy table,

69
00:01:59,611 --> 00:02:00,831
three sets of eight.

70
00:02:00,931 --> 00:02:03,271
Every week, hang a little longer,

71
00:02:03,271 --> 00:02:04,971
and lower a little slower.

72
00:02:05,071 --> 00:02:07,031
Week one, the hang gets easy.

73
00:02:07,111 --> 00:02:09,451
Week two, the negatives get slower.

74
00:02:09,531 --> 00:02:11,931
Week three, you can stop halfway.

75
00:02:12,931 --> 00:02:14,301
And around week four,

76
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:16,111
you pull, and your chin goes over

77
00:02:16,111 --> 00:02:16,891
the bar.

78
00:02:17,891 --> 00:02:19,901
Everyone's watching again.

79
00:02:20,001 --> 00:02:21,961
This time, that's a good thing.

80
00:02:22,041 --> 00:02:23,451
How many pull-ups can you do right

81
00:02:23,451 --> 00:02:24,111
now?

82
00:02:24,191 --> 00:02:25,351
Zero counts.

83
00:02:25,431 --> 00:02:26,471
Tell me in the comments.
